  "text": "Louis Cha (1924-2018), also known by his pen name Jin Yong, was a renowned Chinese author, martial artist, and journalist. He is widely considered one of the greatest wuxia (martial arts fiction) writers of all time.\n\n**Key Facts:**\n\n* **Birth Name:** Zha Liangyong\n* **Pen Name:** Jin Yong (meaning \"Golden Eagle\")\n* **Birth Date:** February 10, 1924\n* **Birthplace:** Haining, Zhejiang, China\n* **Death Date:** October 30, 2018\n* **Nationality:** Chinese\n\n**Literary Career:**\n\n* Wrote 15 wuxia novels, including:\n    * The Legend of the Condor Heroes\n    * The Return of the Condor Heroes\n    * The Heavenly Sword and Dragon Sabre\n    * The Deer and the Cauldron\n    * The Smiling, Proud Wanderer\n* His novels are characterized by intricate plots, memorable characters, and philosophical themes.\n* They have been translated into over 30 languages and have sold over 300 million copies worldwide.\n\n**Other Contributions:**\n\n* Co-founded the Hong Kong newspaper Ming Pao in 1959.\n* Served as its editor-in-chief for over 30 years.\n* Was a renowned calligrapher and painter.\n* Established the Jin Yong Foundation to promote Chinese culture and education.\n\n**Legacy:**\n\n* Louis Cha's wuxia novels have had a profound impact on Chinese literature and popular culture.\n* They have inspired numerous adaptations into films, television series, and video games.\n* He is considered one of the most influential Chinese writers of the 20th century.",
